The ternary operator
PowerShell 7 has a new operator that allows us to construct simple if / else statement pairs in a
single line. On line 15 of our code, we have the following example:
if ($x -lt 4) {
Write-Output ' $x is smaller than 4'
}
else {
<# Action when all if and elseif conditions are false #>

}
We get the output $x is less than 6 . The else statement never gets to run.
